{"duration_api_ms":189050,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"041739c0-157f-4f70-87eb-91a74a5faae5","total_cost_usd":0.243612,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14662,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13177},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14662,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18496,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14662},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18496,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14662,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.243612,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13177,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 10 feasible non-dominated points sit on one curve: D about 3.35 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg (the upper bound), with only flight-path angle varied. Along it, gamma trades heat flux (231k to 278k W/m2) against bondline T (418.7 K to 391.9 K). The binding limits are max_g (about 12, which sets gamma near -3.55) and heatshield_mass_fraction (which sets D near 3.38 at cone 70). Flux is already about 0.1 of the 2.5M reference, so hypervolume gains come almost entirely from lowering T, and only marginally from lowering flux. The local optimum is close, so I mostly refine along its active constraints.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-04a14692e856 (gamma -1.5) to C-b460a0993d3f (gamma -3.55): T falls 418.67 to 391.89 K, flux rises 230.7k to 278.3k, and max_g margin falls 0.232 to 0.004.\",\"Mass-fraction margin at cone 70, bluntness 1.2: 0.0612 at D=3.28 (C-e56e0f295417), 0.0497 at 3.30 (C-cbb67c388863), 0.0207 at 3.35 (C-b460a0993d3f), 0.0090 at 3.37 (C-ddce48f9a845). This is roughly linear at -0.59 per m, so it reaches zero near D=3.385.\",\"Larger D lowers both objectives: C-e56e0f295417 (D 3.28, gamma -3.5) has flux 285.6k and T 393.64, versus C-c4095cf95503 (D 3.35) with 277.0k and 392.38. That is about -123k W/m2 per m and -18 K per m.\",\"Lower bluntness is worse: at D 3.35, gamma -3.5, bluntness 1.0 (C-11dcf14fd72e) gives 287.3k / 393.73 K, versus 277.0k / 392.38 K at 1.2. It also costs about 0.005 of mass margin.\",\"Cone below 70 does not help: C-f901119b3d71 (cone 68, bluntness 1.1) and C-f96d071192f2 (cone 69, bluntness 1.1) are no better than the cone-70 points. The far-off-front points with low cone and low bluntness (C-63aaa0985529, C-50a0a474d0f6) have flux above 500k and higher T.\",\"C-05edbf22eaa2 (bluntness 1.25, cone 70) failed with cd_fore extrapolation, so the surrogate training range ends near bluntness 1.2 at this cone. There are 11 geometry failures, all with cone too small for the bluntness and diameter, so I keep cone at 60 or above.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g in a ballistic entry is set mainly by gamma, so the g limit of 12 caps |gamma| near 3.56. Bondline T falls with steeper gamma (shorter heat pulse) and with larger D (lower ballistic coefficient, so peak heating occurs higher in the atmosphere). Mass fraction grows roughly with D^2 and falls slightly with higher cone angle and bluntness, so D is capped near 3.38 at cone 70. High bluntness and cone 70 give high drag, low flux and low T. Because max_g margin is nearly independent of D and cone, the best design pushes D to the mass limit and gamma to the g limit, and the rest of the front is a gamma sweep at that D. All quantitative predictions come from linear fits to the tabulated rows (the D slopes above and the gamma slopes along the D=3.35 line), not from an independent model.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The D=3.38 to 3.384 points are only 0.001 to 0.003 in mass margin from infeasibility, and gamma -3.56 is 0.002 from the g limit. The linear margin fit could be slightly off, so a few of these may come back infeasible. The bluntness 1.21 probe may hit the surrogate hull and return no metrics. The cone-60 probe is exploratory and likely dominated, and its g and T effects are uncertain. Predicted flux and T come from local linear fits (about 1 K and 3k W/m2 accuracy).\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to the mass limit and gamma to the g limit together. This is the best-T corner of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate for the lowest T on the front. Margins on both g and mass fraction are only about 0.002 to 0.003.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c4095cf95503\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.38 at gamma -3.5 has about 0.01 g margin and 0.003 mass margin, and larger D lowers both flux and T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.84,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the D-to-mass-limit extrapolation at a safe g margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddce48f9a845\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly beyond D=3.38, aiming for about 0.001 mass margin. It tests where the mass limit really lies.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction boundary. If feasible it gives a tiny gain in both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2a4828a90100\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front at gamma -3.4 with the larger D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.84,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Refreshes the front at a mid-high gamma with the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-21b9a186f21d\",\"rationale\":\"The gamma -3.3 front point moved to D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the front around gamma -3.3 through the D effect.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6138656a3bd\",\"rationale\":\"The gamma -3.0 front point at D=3.38. The predicted flux and T are each slightly lower than at D=3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front refinement in the middle of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4370b59bae5e\",\"rationale\":\"The gamma -2.5 front point at D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front refinement at moderate gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3cfec4d90b09\",\"rationale\":\"The gamma -2.0 front point at D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front refinement at shallow gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-04a14692e856\",\"rationale\":\"The shallowest-gamma end of the front at D=3.38. It gives the lowest flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":418.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front at the low-flux end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab6fb1629c20\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the front gap between gamma -1.6 and -2.0 at D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front in the shallow-gamma region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4370b59bae5e\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the front gap between gamma -2.0 and -2.5 at D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-76a81df51d42\",\"rationale\":\"The gamma -2.75 front point at D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front refinement at mid gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f901119b3d71\",\"rationale\":\"Tests whether cone 68 at bluntness 1.2 and D=3.38 gives any g or T benefit. Earlier cone-68 and cone-69 rows used bluntness 1.1 only.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the cone-angle effect at the high-bluntness corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f96d071192f2\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69 with bluntness 1.2 at D=3.36 and gamma -3.5 tests cone sensitivity near the corner while keeping mass margin around 0.014.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether cone 70 is truly optimal.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c4095cf95503\",\"rationale\":\"Slight bluntness increase to 1.21. Higher bluntness lowers flux and raises mass margin. It probes the surrogate hull edge, since 1.25 failed.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the bluntness range can be extended. It may return an extrapolation failure.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory lower cone (60) at D 3.3 and gamma -3.55, to test the cone effect on g, flux and T with a mass margin of about 0.04.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether lower cone gives a g benefit that allows steeper gamma. Earlier low-cone rows suggested a small g reduction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly steeper gamma at D=3.36, which has a safer mass margin of about 0.014. Predicted g margin is only about 0.001.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g boundary with a safe mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate point at D 3.37 and gamma -3.56.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A hedge between the aggressive and safe corner candidates.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c4095cf95503\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate D and gamma (3.375, -3.53) with about 0.006 g margin and 0.005 mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely feasible, and improves T slightly on the current best front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ddce48f9a845\",\"rationale\":\"Front point at gamma -3.45 with D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front near the g limit at the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":145746,"type":"result","duration_ms":189286,"uuid":"b6002d29-363c-4455-b4d9-da34a5eb8759","ttft_stream_ms":3003,"time_to_request_ms":208,"first_content_frame_ms":3004,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_